## 📁 **PROJECT STRUCTURE**

### Standard MuleSoft API Project

```
{project-name}/
├── pom.xml                          # Maven configuration
├── mule-artifact.json               # Mule artifact descriptor
├── src/main/mule/
│   ├── interface.xml                # API interface flows
│   ├── global/
│   │   ├── global-config.xml        # Global configurations
│   │   └── global-error-handler.xml # Error handling
│   ├── implementation/              # Endpoint implementations
│   └── subflows/                    # Reusable subflows
├── src/main/resources/
│   ├── config/{env}.yaml            # Environment configs
│   ├── dw/                          # DataWeave files
│   └── api/                         # RAML specifications
└── src/test/munit/                  # MUnit tests
```

### Eclipse/Studio Configuration Files
<!-- Integrated: 2026-01-10 -->

Generate Eclipse/Studio configuration files to ensure projects open in Mule Perspective (not Java).

**Required Files:**

`.project` - Use `muleStudioBuilder` and `muleStudioNature`:
```xml
<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<projectDescription>
    <name>{project-name}</name>
    <buildSpec>
        <buildCommand>
            <name>org.eclipse.jdt.core.javabuilder</name>
        </buildCommand>
        <buildCommand>
            <name>org.mule.tooling.core.muleStudioBuilder</name>
        </buildCommand>
    </buildSpec>
    <natures>
        <nature>org.mule.tooling.core.muleStudioNature</nature>
        <nature>org.eclipse.jdt.core.javanature</nature>
    </natures>
</projectDescription>
```

`.classpath` - Include all POM connectors with exact versions, Mule Runtime, source folders:
```xml
<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<classpath>
    <classpathentry kind="con" path="MULE_LIB/com.mulesoft.munit/munit-tools/3.1.0"/>
    <classpathentry kind="con" path="MULE_LIB/com.mulesoft.munit/munit-runner/3.1.0"/>
    <classpathentry kind="con" path="MULE_LIB/{groupId}/{artifactId}/{version}"/>
    <classpathentry kind="con" path="org.eclipse.jdt.launching.JRE_CONTAINER"/>
    <classpathentry exported="true" kind="con" path="MULE_RUNTIME/org.mule.tooling.server.4.7.ee"/>
    <classpathentry kind="src" path="src/main/mule"/>
    <classpathentry kind="src" path="src/main/resources"/>
    <classpathentry kind="src" output="target/test-classes" path="src/test/java"/>
    <classpathentry kind="src" output="target/test-classes" path="src/test/resources"/>
    <classpathentry kind="src" output="target/test-classes" path="src/test/munit"/>
    <classpathentry kind="output" path="target/classes"/>
</classpath>
```

`.settings/org.mulesoft.exportwizardsettings.prefs`:
```
eclipse.preferences.version=1
```

**Critical Rules:**
- Connector versions in `.classpath` MUST match POM `<dependencies>`
- Runtime version MUST match POM `<mule.version>` property
- Include MUnit dependencies if MUnit is in POM

### POM `<name>` Element Must Match `<artifactId>`
<!-- Integrated: 2026-01-10 -->

The `<name>` element in `pom.xml` MUST match the `<artifactId>` exactly for consistency with MuleSoft project conventions and to avoid potential IDE/build issues.

```xml
<!-- ✅ CORRECT -->
<artifactId>customer-notification-publisher-sapi</artifactId>
<name>customer-notification-publisher-sapi</name>

<!-- ❌ INCORRECT -->
<artifactId>customer-notification-publisher-sapi</artifactId>
<name>Customer Notification Publisher System API</name>
```

**Why**: Matches working example project structure, ensures consistency, prevents potential build/IDE issues.

