    </dependency>
</dependencies>
```

**⚠️ Runtime Modules - Do NOT Declare as Dependencies**
<!-- Integrated: 2026-01-10 -->

DataWeave (`ee:transform`) and Scheduler (`scheduler:scheduler`) are part of Mule Runtime 4.6+ and **MUST NOT** be declared as explicit dependencies. Adding them causes build failures when they require authentication or aren't available in public repositories.

```xml
<!-- ❌ INCORRECT - Do NOT add these -->
<dependency>
    <groupId>org.mule.modules</groupId>
    <artifactId>mule-dw-module</artifactId>
    <version>2.2.0</version>
    <classifier>mule-plugin</classifier>
</dependency>
<dependency>
    <groupId>org.mule.modules</groupId>
    <artifactId>mule-scheduler-module</artifactId>
    <version>1.1.0</version>
    <classifier>mule-plugin</classifier>
</dependency>

<!-- ✅ CORRECT - These are runtime modules, no dependency needed -->
<!-- DataWeave (ee:transform) and Scheduler are part of Mule Runtime 4.6+ -->
```

**Why**: Reduces unnecessary dependencies, avoids authentication issues, cleaner POM files, matches MuleSoft best practices.

### Maven Plugin Configuration
<!-- Integrated: 2026-01-10 -->

The Mule Maven plugin **MUST** use groupId `org.mule.tools.maven` (NOT `org.apache.maven.plugins`) to prevent "Unresolveable build extension" errors.

```xml
<!-- ✅ CORRECT -->
<plugin>
    <groupId>org.mule.tools.maven</groupId>
    <artifactId>mule-maven-plugin</artifactId>
    <version>4.3.0</version>
    <extensions>true</extensions>
    <configuration>
        <classifier>mule-application</classifier>
    </configuration>
</plugin>

<!-- ❌ INCORRECT -->
<plugin>
    <groupId>org.apache.maven.plugins</groupId>
    <artifactId>mule-maven-plugin</artifactId>
    <version>4.3.0</version>
    <extensions>true</extensions>
</plugin>
```

**Why**: Correct Maven plugin resolution, prevents build extension errors, ensures proper Mule application packaging.

