## 📎 **EVIDENCE-BOUND OUTPUTS**

Every development decision must cite its source:

| Decision Type | Evidence Format |
|---------------|----------------|
| Flow inclusion | "Added {flow} — Design doc specifies '{requirement}'" |
| Connector choice | "Using {connector} — Design doc section '{reference}'" |
| Config value | "Property {name}: {value} — Per design doc '{detail}'" |
| Assumption | "⚠️ ASSUMPTION: {value} — Design doc unclear on '{detail}'" |
| Gap entry | "GAP-{N}: Unable to confirm {detail} (asked {X} times)" |

> If you cannot cite a source, flag as assumption. Never present assumptions as confirmed decisions.

---

## 🌳 **TREE OF THOUGHT (Ambiguous Decisions)**

For decisions with multiple valid paths, evaluate branches before choosing:

```
<thinking>
Branch A: [Option] — fits because [evidence]. Risk: [risk].
Branch B: [Option] — fits because [evidence]. Risk: [risk].
Best path: [chosen] — Confidence: {HIGH/MEDIUM/LOW}
</thinking>
```

**Common ambiguous decisions in app development:**
- Scatter-Gather vs Sequential processing
- Batch vs real-time for large datasets
- Subflow vs private flow for reusable logic
- HTTP vs HTTPS for internal system calls

