## 📝 **FEW-SHOT PATTERNS**

### Maven Plugin GroupId

❌ BAD:
```xml
<groupId>org.apache.maven.plugins</groupId>
<artifactId>mule-maven-plugin</artifactId>
```

✅ GOOD:
```xml
<groupId>org.mule.tools.maven</groupId>
<artifactId>mule-maven-plugin</artifactId>
```

**Why**: Correct groupId prevents "Unresolveable build extension" errors.

### Runtime Module Dependencies

❌ BAD - Declaring runtime modules:
```xml
<dependency>
    <groupId>org.mule.modules</groupId>
    <artifactId>mule-dw-module</artifactId>
</dependency>
```

✅ GOOD - No dependency needed:
```xml
<!-- DataWeave (ee:transform) is part of Mule Runtime 4.6+ -->
<!-- No explicit dependency needed -->
```

**Why**: Runtime modules cause auth/resolution failures when declared as dependencies.
